# Lab 4: Protecting the API
# Paste a token from dotnet user-jwts (Lab 3).
@host = https://localhost:7001
@ticketId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@alice = paste-alice-token-here

### Create a ticket as alice. Send this 21 times in a minute: the 21st is 429.
# (Or use "Trip the rate limiter" in the lab client.)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Again", "description": "And again.", "priority": "Low", "requesterId": "alice" }

### Look at the response headers: nosniff, Referrer-Policy, Content-Security-Policy
GET {{host}}/api/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{alice}}

### CORS preflight from the support site: allowed
OPTIONS {{host}}/api/v1/tickets
Origin: https://support.ticketing.example
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
Access-Control-Request-Headers: authorization,content-type

### CORS preflight from anywhere else: no Access-Control-Allow-Origin
OPTIONS {{host}}/api/v1/tickets
Origin: https://evil.example
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
